--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. PURPOSE AND INTENDED USE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

HUGINN is a security testing framework designed exclusively for:

  (a) Authorized penetration testing engagements;
  (b) Bug bounty programs conducted under published rules of engagement;
  (c) Internal security audits performed on systems you own or control;
  (d) Security research conducted with explicit written authorization from
      the owner of every system tested;
  (e) Educational use in controlled laboratory environments (e.g., DVWA,
      OWASP WebGoat, PortSwigger Web Security Academy, HackTheBox,
      TryHackMe, and similar deliberately vulnerable training platforms).

Any use outside these categories is STRICTLY PROHIBITED.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. AUTHORIZATION REQUIREMENT
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

You represent and warrant that, prior to using the Software against any
system, network, application, or service:

  (a) You have obtained EXPLICIT, DOCUMENTED, WRITTEN AUTHORIZATION from the
      legitimate owner or operator of the target, specifying the scope of
      testing, the timeframe, and the permitted activities;

  (b) Your use complies with all applicable local, state, national, and
      international laws, including but not limited to the Computer Fraud
      and Abuse Act (18 U.S.C. § 1030) in the United States, the Computer
      Misuse Act 1990 in the United Kingdom, the Cybercrime Convention
      (Budapest Convention), the General Data Protection Regulation (EU)
      2016/679, and any equivalent legislation in your jurisdiction;

  (c) You will not use the Software to access, alter, damage, disable,
      overload, or impair any system without authorization;

  (d) You will respect the scope limitations, rate limits, and rules of
      engagement of any bug bounty program, penetration testing contract,
      or research agreement under which you operate.

